==English==

{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|iːzə(r)}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|geyser}} (In some dialects)

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|informal|chiefly|British|dated in US|lang=en}} A [[male]] person.
#* '''1922''', [[w:P. G. Wodehouse|P. G. Wodehouse]], ''Right Ho, Jeeves'', ch. 19:
#*: You are a silly young '''geezer'''.
# {{context|UK|slang|lang=en}} Informal address to a [[male]].
#:''Hi '''geezer''', you alright?''
# {{context|informal|chiefly|US|sometimes|mildly|derogatory|lang=en}} An [[old]] person, usually a male.
#* '''2000''', Moira McDonald, "[http://community.seattletimes.nwsource.com/archive/?date=20000825&slug=4038797 Outtakes]," ''Seattle Times'', 25 Aug. (retrieved 6 Sep. 2008):
#*: The technical term for a female '''geezer''' is "old broad," but this is irrelevant, as nobody in Hollywood makes films about women over 55.
# {{context|British|lang=en}} A device for [[boil]]ing water for such [[domestic]] uses as heating or washing; a [[boiler]]. The normal spelling is water {{term|geyser}}.

